        "body": "In trying to cull down my dataset, a few times I've attempted to delete... a lot of records.\n\nEvery time I've done this, the app soft crashes. On a reload, it _slowly_ loads data - response times go up to around 30s and memory starts to approach 8gb which AFAIK is the cap of a Node.js process in more modern Node.js versions thanks to V8 memory management.\n\nThe most recent way I've situation I encountered this under was with `site.standard.document`, trying to delete what seems like a lot of records that I backfilled at one point. When I delete all records, the modal processes for a bit then _seemingly_ silently fails and allows me to click the button again. Every time this has happened, I've clicked the button again and then have refreshed the app. At that point, it loads... partially as it seems to be recovering from silent failures.\n\nHere's perf stats from my HappyView instance while this was happening:\n\n<img width=\"786\" height=\"723\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/03d752dd-f131-4d67-8b11-f123af8dd505\" />\n\n<img width=\"787\" height=\"404\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1d41098e-8931-4e83-ab56-0efed40fad9c\" />",
